# agent-disk-cleanup per-directory retention policies
#
# Copy to policies.conf (next to install.sh) and edit, or point POLICIES_FILE at
# it. Each non-comment line is:
#
#     <glob>  <keep>  <inactive_min>  <days>
#
#   keep          the N most recent top-level sessions in a matching directory
#                 are kept (0 = keep none). Their sub-sessions are kept too.
#   inactive_min  never prune a session idle for fewer than this many minutes.
#                 This protects sessions that are open/frozen but not writing.
#   days          age cutoff in days (0 = count-only, no time floor).
#
# The FIRST matching glob wins, so put specific rules before the catch-all.
# Directories with no matching rule use the cleanup.conf defaults
# (KEEP_RECENT_SESSIONS / INACTIVE_MINUTES / RETENTION_DAYS).
#
# Sessions referenced by a running opencode process (by session id in argv or by
# working directory) are always protected, regardless of these rules.

# Disposable agent working directories: keep nothing once idle for 48h.
*/working-directories/slot-*   0   2880   0

# Everything else: keep the last 10 sessions per directory, 48h idle grace.
*                              10  2880   0
